.TH CHTTP_BASIC_AUTH_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_basic_auth_mp \- build an HTTP Basic auth header value with a custom allocator
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttp.h>

char *chttp_basic_auth_mp(ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp,
                          const char *username, const char *password);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Builds a "Basic <base64(username:password)>" header value per RFC
7617. Produces only the header VALUE, not the "Authorization: " key
part; pass the result directly to chttp_request_set_header(req,
"authorization", ...) or the chttpsvr equivalent.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
mp        Custom allocator, or NULL for malloc/free.
username  Username. Must not be NULL; may be empty.
password  Password. Must not be NULL; may be empty.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Newly allocated "Basic <base64>" string on success.
NULL on allocation failure, or if username or password is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_basic_auth (3),
.BR chttp_base64_encode_mp (3),
.BR chttp_request_set_header (3)
